Data Analysis Cohort 2: Full Curriculum
Vixora Academy · 16 weeks · Draft v1 for review
Course Overview
This is a practical, beginner-to-professional course that takes students from raw data to clear business insight. Students learn Excel, statistics, SQL and Python, get a short introduction to Power BI, and learn to use AI tools to work faster. The course ends with a capstone project and a portfolio they can show to employers and clients.
* Duration: 16 weeks
* Format: Online / Physical (hybrid)
* Level: Beginner to professional
* Pricing: ₦30,000
* Certificate: Awarded on completion of the capstone project
Learning Outcomes
By the end of the course, students will be able to:
* Follow a structured analysis workflow, from business question to recommendation
* Clean, organize and analyze data in Excel, SQL and Python
* Apply core statistics to interpret data correctly
* Build clear charts and dashboards in Excel, Python and Power BI
* Use AI tools to speed up analysis while checking the results for accuracy
* Present findings as a clear story to non-technical audiences
* Complete a portfolio-ready capstone project
Tools Used
Excel (or Google Sheets), a free SQL tool (such as SQLite or MySQL), Python in Google Colab / Jupyter (Pandas, Matplotlib, Seaborn), Power BI Desktop (introduction only), and AI assistants (ChatGPT, Claude or similar).
Course Structure
* Phase 1: Excel (Weeks 1-5): workflow, Excel, cleaning, pivot tables, dashboards
* Phase 2: Statistics and SQL (Weeks 6-8)
* Phase 3: Python (Weeks 9-11)
* Phase 4: Power BI and AI (Weeks 12-13)
* Phase 5: Application and Career (Weeks 14-16)
Assessment (Proposed)
* Weekly practical assignments
* Mid-course practical test (Excel, SQL)
* Capstone project: report, dashboard and presentation
* Certificate issued on completing all weekly deliverables and the capstone
Week 1: Introduction to Data Analysis and Tools Setup
Objectives
* Understand what data analysis is and what analysts do
* Learn the analysis workflow
* Set up all tools for the course
Topics
* What data analysis is, and the types of analysis
* Analyst roles and career paths
* The analysis workflow: ask, prepare, process, analyze, share, act
* Types of data: structured and unstructured, quantitative and qualitative
* Tools overview, and setting up Excel, Google Colab and a portfolio folder
Hands-on
* Classify sample datasets by type
* Turn a vague business problem into a clear analysis question
Deliverable: one-page analysis question brief
Week 2: Excel Fundamentals
Objectives
* Work confidently in Excel
* Use core formulas and lookups
Topics
* Interface, data entry, formatting and tables
* Formulas and functions: SUM, AVERAGE, COUNT, MIN, MAX, IF
* Relative and absolute references
* Lookups: XLOOKUP / VLOOKUP
* Sorting and filtering
Hands-on
* Build a sales tracker with formulas and lookups
Deliverable: completed sales workbook
Week 3: Data Cleaning and Preparation
Objectives
* Spot and fix common data quality problems
* Document cleaning decisions
Topics
* Duplicates, missing values and inconsistent entries
* Text functions: TRIM, LEFT, RIGHT, CONCAT, TEXTSPLIT
* Date and number formatting
* Data validation
* Introduction to Power Query for cleaning
Hands-on
* Clean a deliberately messy customer dataset
Deliverable: cleaned dataset plus a short change log
Week 4: Data Analysis with Excel
Objectives
* Summarize large datasets quickly
* Answer business questions with Pivot Tables
Topics
* Pivot Tables, grouping and slicers
* SUMIFS, COUNTIFS, AVERAGEIFS
* Calculated fields
* Descriptive summaries and basic trend analysis
Hands-on
* Analyze a year of sales data by product, region and month
Deliverable: pivot summary report with three insights
Week 5: Excel Dashboards and Data Visualization
Objectives
* Choose the right chart for the question
* Build a clean, interactive dashboard
Topics
* Chart types and when to use each
* Design principles: clarity, color, layout
* Common visualization mistakes
* Interactive dashboards with slicers
Hands-on
* Build a sales performance dashboard
Deliverable: Excel dashboard
Week 6: Statistics Essentials for Analysts
Objectives
* Understand the statistics behind everyday analysis
* Avoid common interpretation errors
Topics
* Mean, median, mode, range
* Variance and standard deviation
* Distributions and outliers
* Correlation versus causation
* Sampling, bias and introductory hypothesis testing
Hands-on
* Run summary statistics and correlation analysis in Excel
Deliverable: statistics worksheet with written interpretations
Week 7: SQL Basics
Objectives
* Understand how databases are organized
* Retrieve and summarize data with SQL
Topics
* Databases, tables, rows, columns, primary and foreign keys
* SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, LIMIT, DISTINCT
* Aggregate functions: COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX
* GROUP BY
Hands-on
* Query a sample store database to answer business questions
Deliverable: SQL query set with answers
Week 8: SQL Intermediate
Objectives
* Combine data from multiple tables
* Write more advanced queries
Topics
* INNER and LEFT joins
* HAVING and filtering aggregated results
* Subqueries and CASE statements
* Date functions
* Introduction to CTEs
Hands-on
* Solve multi-table business questions (top customers, monthly revenue, repeat buyers)
Deliverable: SQL assignment plus mid-course practical test
Week 9: Python Fundamentals for Data
Objectives
* Write basic Python for data work
* Work comfortably in notebooks
Topics
* Google Colab / Jupyter basics
* Variables, data types, lists and dictionaries
* Conditionals, loops and functions
* Importing libraries
Hands-on
* Write small scripts that process lists of sales and customer records
Deliverable: Python practice notebook
Week 10: Data Manipulation with Pandas
Objectives
* Load, clean and reshape data in Python
* Repeat Excel and SQL tasks with Pandas
Topics
* DataFrames and Series
* Loading CSV and Excel files
* Selecting, filtering and sorting
* Handling missing values and duplicates
* groupby, merge and creating new columns
* Exporting results
Hands-on
* Clean and summarize the Week 3 dataset in Pandas
Deliverable: cleaning and analysis notebook
Week 11: Exploratory Data Analysis and Visualization in Python
Objectives
* Explore a new dataset systematically
* Create clear charts in Python
Topics
* Matplotlib and Seaborn basics
* Distributions, relationships and outliers
* Correlation heatmaps
* An EDA checklist
Hands-on
* Run a full EDA on a real-world dataset
Deliverable: EDA notebook with written insights
Week 12: Power BI Introduction
Objectives
* Understand where Power BI fits in an analyst's toolkit
* Build a simple dashboard
Topics
* What Power BI is and when to use it
* Interface and data connection
* Basic transformation with Power Query
* Core visuals, filters and slicers
* Building a one-page dashboard
Hands-on
* Rebuild the Week 5 dashboard in Power BI
Deliverable: one-page Power BI dashboard
This week is an introduction only. Advanced Power BI (DAX, data modeling) is outside this course.
